  "settingsSellerSection": "مشخصات فروشنده",
  "@settingsSellerSection": {
    "description": "Section heading for the user own business details on the settings screen (schema v5, D-077). These are printed as the seller block of the invoice. Named «مشخصات فروشنده» rather than «کسب و کار من» so the heading uses the same word the document does: the user should be able to see which part of the printed page this section fills in."
  },
  "settingsSellerEmpty": "ثبت نشده",
  "@settingsSellerEmpty": {
    "description": "Shown as the value of a seller row that has not been filled in. Deliberately the same admission wording the invoice uses for an unrecorded figure: it says the value was never given, rather than leaving a blank that reads as data which failed to load."
  },
  "settingsSellerConsequence": "تا زمانی که نام کسب‌وکار را وارد نکنید، بخش «فروشنده» روی فاکتور چاپ نمی‌شود.",
  "@settingsSellerConsequence": {
    "description": "The one sentence that makes an empty seller impossible to be surprised by (D-077). Shown under the seller section whenever no business name is stored. It states the consequence -- the block is omitted from the printed invoice -- rather than nagging: an empty seller does not block issuing or printing, it is the user document and their call, so the only obligation is that they were told. Carries a ZWNJ twice, so it exercises the D-073 atom on a real screen string."
  },
  "settingsSellerEditTitle": "ویرایش مشخصات فروشنده",
  "@settingsSellerEditTitle": {},
  "settingsSellerEditTooltip": "ویرایش مشخصات فروشنده",
  "@settingsSellerEditTooltip": {
    "description": "Tooltip on the edit control in the seller section header. Deliberately the full phrase rather than the bare edit the invoicing section uses: with two edit controls on one screen, a tooltip that does not say which section it opens is no help at all."
  },
  "settingsSellerFieldName": "نام کسب‌وکار",
  "@settingsSellerFieldName": {
    "description": "The seller business name. The identifying field of the block: the document prints no seller block without it, and the form requires it as soon as any other seller field is filled."
  },
  "settingsSellerFieldNameHint": "همان‌گونه که باید روی فاکتور چاپ شود.",
  "@settingsSellerFieldNameHint": {},
  "settingsSellerFieldAddress": "نشانی",
  "@settingsSellerFieldAddress": {},
  "settingsSellerFieldPhone": "تلفن",
  "@settingsSellerFieldPhone": {
    "description": "The seller telephone. Deliberately a different label from the customer mobile field: a business published number is as often a landline with an area code, and it is stored as typed rather than normalized to the 09xxxxxxxxx mobile shape."
  },
  "settingsSellerFieldPhoneHint": "همان‌گونه که وارد می‌کنید ذخیره و چاپ می‌شود.",
  "@settingsSellerFieldPhoneHint": {
    "description": "Says the number is kept exactly as typed. Worth saying because the customer mobile field does normalize, so a user who has met that field would reasonably expect this one to as well."
  },
  "settingsErrorSellerNameRequired": "برای چاپ مشخصات فروشنده، نام کسب‌وکار لازم است. برای حذف کامل این بخش، همه فیلدها را خالی بگذارید.",
  "@settingsErrorSellerNameRequired": {
    "description": "Validation error when a seller field is filled but the name is not. Reported, never clamped (D-027): a seller block carrying an economic ID and no name is a fragment rather than an identification. The second sentence is what stops the rule becoming a trap -- it says how to get OUT of the section, because a user who wants no seller block at all must be able to empty it."
  },
