  "invoiceCancelAction": "ابطال فاکتور",
  "@invoiceCancelAction": {
    "description": "The menu item and the confirming button, deliberately the same words. Distinct from actionCancel, which is a dialog's «انصراف» and means the opposite here."
  },
  "invoiceCancelTitle": "این فاکتور باطل شود؟",
  "@invoiceCancelTitle": {},
  "invoiceCancelBody": "فاکتور حذف نمی‌شود؛ در سوابق می‌ماند و «باطل شده» علامت می‌خورد. شماره آن آزاد نمی‌شود و به هیچ فاکتور دیگری داده نمی‌شود. ابطال برگشت‌پذیر نیست و فاکتور پس از آن قابل ویرایش نیست؛ برای اصلاح، فاکتور تازه‌ای صادر کنید.",
  "@invoiceCancelBody": {
    "description": "Cancellation is the correction path, so the copy states what it does and what it does not do before the user commits: the record stays, the number stays spent (D-013), and editing is still not the way back. A confirmation that only asks «are you sure» is one people learn to dismiss."
  },
  "invoiceCancelPaymentsNote": "{amount} {unit} پرداختی که تاکنون ثبت شده حذف نمی‌شود و بازگردانده نمی‌شود. ابطال، فاکتور را باطل می‌کند نه پولی را که دریافت شده است.",
  "@invoiceCancelPaymentsNote": {
    "description": "Shown only when the invoice actually carries payments (D-060's rule). Cancelling never touches the payments table (D-061), and a user cancelling a part-paid invoice must be told that before committing, not discover it afterwards. The unit is a placeholder because the user chooses it (D-117).",
    "placeholders": { "amount": { "type": "String" }, "unit": { "type": "String" } }
  },
  "invoiceCancelThenDeleteNote": "پس از ابطال، می‌توانید این فاکتور را به‌کلی حذف کنید.",
  "@invoiceCancelThenDeleteNote": {
    "description": "Shown on every cancellation dialog. Closes the discoverability half of D-105: deletion is offered only after cancellation, so a user looking for a way to clear a mistaken or test invoice would otherwise see only the cancel action and conclude the document is permanent -- which is what was reported from the phone. This is the one place they are standing when the answer is relevant."
  },

